# The scenes of the differential-testing deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# differential-testing.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in differential-testing.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: the old calculator
note "The *old* postage calculator: a chain of ifs, in use for years. Its answers are the prices the business means."
show LegacyPostage 8 23 "the old calculator"

## Scene 2: the rewrite
note "The code under test: the *rewrite*. It reads the same prices from a price list."
show RewrittenPostage 17 30 "the rewrite" --zoom 22-23

## Scene 3: the rewrite's own tests
note "The rewrite's *own tests*: one typical weight from each row of the price list."
show RewriteExamplesTest 8 16 "the rewrite's own tests" --zoom 12

## Scene 4: the differential test
note "A *differential* test: ask both calculators about every weight, and list where they disagree."
show OldAndNewAgreeTest 22 37 "the differential test" --mark 25,37
show OldAndNewAgreeTest 41 59 "every weight in the band, asked of both" --zoom 42-43,58

## Scene 5: the comparison finds a gap
note "Run the tests against the rewrite as it is today:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:differential-testing:test -Pcode=today"
callout "Every example passes. The comparison finds 50 weights, 451 g to 500 g, where the rewrite charges more."

## Scene 6: the corrected price list
note "The price list, checked against the printed one:"
show PriceList 8 12 "the price list" --zoom 9-12
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:differential-testing:test"
callout "The rewrite agrees with the old calculator on all 5,000 weights. Now the old one can go."
